From a3a5835427d8c86b92d7d7b8f62fe5b327f8e4a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Che Haijun <chehaijun@Mac.localdomain>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:15:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(coding): inline coding popup and code-coloured
 highlights

Selecting text now opens a small box anchored to the selection instead of a bar
pinned to the bottom of the reading pane, and the keyword field replaces the
code dropdown: typing filters the codebook, Enter applies the top match, and if
nothing matches Enter creates the code and applies it in one step. A "more
options" button still opens the full dialog for memos.

Highlights now carry the code's colour. Each span takes its background from the
shallowest active code (the theme) and its underline from the deepest (the leaf
code), so a two-level codebook reads as two levels of emphasis. Previously every
highlight was the same fixed yellow and the code name only appeared on hover.

Also fixes a latent problem: overlapping codes on the same span used to collapse
into a single <mark>, so a span coded twice showed one label. Colours are now
derived from all active codes.

The pending selection is kept visible with the CSS Custom Highlight API, because
focusing the keyword field clears the native selection. The popup shrinks its
suggestion list when the viewport cannot fit it above or below the selection, and
re-anchors on scroll and resize.

The bottom selection bar, its slot and its CSS are removed.
