-/* --- Fix: the coding selection bar was unreachable ---------------------------
-   .selection-bar used position:sticky inside #selection-slot, a wrapper whose
-   height equals the bar itself. Sticky cannot move an element outside its own
-   containing block, so the bar had zero travel and stayed at the very bottom of
-   the scroll content. In a long transcript (e.g. 72 segments / ~15,000px) it
-   rendered far below the visible area, so selecting text mid-document showed no
-   "Apply code" control at all.
-   Moving the sticky context onto #selection-slot makes its containing block the
-   scroll container (.document-pane), so the bar pins to the bottom of the pane.
-   pointer-events keeps the empty slot from swallowing clicks. */
-.selection-bar{position:static;gap:9px;margin:8px 24px;padding:10px 12px;font-size:12px}
-#selection-slot{position:sticky;bottom:0;z-index:6;pointer-events:none}
-#selection-slot:empty{display:none}
-#selection-slot>*{pointer-events:auto}
